and researchers\nStaff\nInstitutions and companies\nHeader\nLogin\nEN\nIT\nToggle language menu\nSearch\nPh.D. programme in Mechanical Engineering\nSkip to main content\nAcademic Board\nCareer opportunities\nStudy plan\nResearch topics\nCommittees\nAdvisory Board\nRegulations\nStudents\nAlumni\nBreadcrumb\nHome\nEducation\nPh.D. programmes and Postgraduate School\nPh.D. programmes\nMechanical Engineering\nProgramme overview\nImmagine\nThe PhD programme in Mechanical Engineering has the goal of forming researchers and professionals who are able to carry out advanced research & development activities in the field of system and structural mechanics, mechanics of controlled devices, machines and fluids. PhD education focuses on functional and structural design, control of machines and machine elements, mechanical system analysis in a broad sense, and their application in the industrial sector.\nDuring the programme, students attend courses on theoretical methodologies, numerical instruments and experimental techniques suitable to the understanding of the physical phenomena and their interpretation. The programme offers III-level courses to improve specialized knowledge in the field.\nPhD programme promotes international experiences, organizing secondments at the foreign universities and research centres which collaborate with the concerned Department (DIMEAS: Department of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering), promoting the attendance in international congresses, and offering seminars or excellence courses given by renowned international scholars.\nGo to the call for applications\nKey information\nType of programme:\nPhD programme\nDepartment:\nDepartment of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering\nCoordinator:\nVIGLIANI ALESSANDRO\nVice coordinator:\nPERONI LORENZO\nAdmissions:\nOpen, through competitive selection\nTitolo\nContacts\nContatti e-mail\nTitolo\nStudent office\nE-mail\ndimeas.dottorati@polito.it\nTitolo\nRepresentative of PhD candidates\nE-mail\nstefano.tomassi@polito.it\nNavigate this section\nAcademic Board\nCareer opportunities\nStudy plan\nResearch topics\nCommittees\nAdvisory Board\nRegulations\nStudents\nAlumni\nSince 1859 our students have been changing the world. Support their idea of the future.\nDonate\nSkip to next section\nPi\u00e8 di pagina\nContact\nMaps\nEmergency\nPrivacy policy\nOpen competitions and selections\nCalls for tenders\nIT services\nAlumni\nSign up for PoliTO newsletter\nAdministration Transparency\nAlbo online\nAtti di notifica\nDichiarazione di accessibilit\u00e0\nCookie settings\nPolitecnico di Torino | Corso Duca degli Abruzzi, 24 | 10129 Torino, ITALY | P.IVA/C.F. 00518460019 | PEC politecnicoditorino@pec.polito.it\nSocial\nInstagram\nLinkedin\nFacebook\nTiktok\nX-Twitter\nYoutube\nTelegram\nThreads\nWechat\nOndeQuadre", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://www.polito.it/en/education/phd-programmes-and-postgraduate-school/phd-programmes/mechanical-engineering#main-content"], ["Services Status", "https://status.polito.it/"], ["Login", "https://idp.polito.it/home"], ["IT", "https://www.polito.it/didattica/dottorato-di-ricerca-e-scuola-di-specializzazione/corsi-attivi/ingegneria-meccanica"], ["", "https://www.polito.it/en"], ["Skip to main content", "https://www.polito.it/en/education/phd-programmes-and-postgraduate-school/phd-programmes/mechanical-engineering#main-content"], ["PoliTO", "https://www.polito.it/en/polito"], ["Go to page PoliTO", "https://www.polito.it/en/polito"], ["About us", "https://www.polito.it/en/polito/about-us"], ["Politecnico at a glance", "https://www.polito.it/en/polito/politecnico-at-a-glance"], ["Strategy", "https://www.polito.it/en/polito/strategy"], ["An international University", "https://www.polito.it/en/polito/an-international-university"], ["Equity, welfare and inclusion", "https://www.polito.it/en/polito/equity-welfare-and-inclusion"], ["Sustainable campus", "https://www.polito.it/en/polito/sustainable-campus"], ["Career Hub", "https://www.polito.it